DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash reference inference code
--------------------------------------------

DeepSeek-AI published DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash together with reference inference
code (model.py, engram.py, kernel.py). Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek. The MIT
terms that accompany it are in LICENSE-DEEPSEEK and at
https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/blob/main/LICENSE.

exllamav3/architecture/dsv41/engram_torch.py adapts that reference's n-gram
hashing and compressed token map to a bounded lookback window.
exllamav3/architecture/dsv41/engram.py and tests/dsv41_ref/engram_hash.py
carry parts of its engram.py through vLLM's port listed above: the hash
multipliers (compute_hash_multipliers), the prime bucket layout
(EngramLayout) and the n-gram hash (NgramHashState).
exllamav3/modules/dsv41_rounding.py reimplements in torch the activation
rounding of its kernel.py (act_quant and fp4_act_quant, with E8M0 and E4M3
scales).

These tests transcribe parts of the reference as oracles and name the
transcribed functions in their descriptions:

  tests/test_dsv41_select_.py
  tests/test_dsv41_engram_ref_.py
  tests/test_dsv41_engram_gpu_.py
  tests/test_dsv41_engram_fwd_gpu_.py
  tests/test_dsv41_qkv_front_gpu_.py

The other V4.1 files describe the reference semantics they follow in their
module descriptions.


