  tests/dsv41_ref/engram_tables.py
    patch/engram_helper.py (DiskEngramTable._open and _read_rows)
      commit 8fda87b2a0c3b4db097380c2d55af9f842828938
      SHA256 f97e085c0f308df25e058cf55484ffc4357f91489cb921174911c116cf9128ec

EngramTable._fd and EngramTable._pread_rows adapt its threaded row reader: one
os.preadv per row with a short-read loop, POSIX_FADV_RANDOM on the descriptor,
and the rows split into chunks submitted to a thread pool (32 threads and 16
rows per task by default), read inline when a batch fits in one chunk.
Modified for exllamav3: numpy buffers, one cached descriptor per shard file,
the row and file named in the short-read error, and constructor arguments in
place of environment variables. It reached this project through
https://github.com/sfxnz/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-EXL3-vLLM-2x-DGX-Spark at
460ac89c7df1eea4db8a731f1feb807f1584f359 (docker/patch/engram_disk.py), which
carries the same reader with renamed identifiers and credits its origin.
